  "title": "Model retirement check: tested fallback chain for VISION_MODEL and DECIDE_MODEL, dated note",
  "spec": "Why: P0-11. Planner check 2026-10-06 of platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/model-deprecations: claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 is Active, no deprecation notice, tentative retirement \"not sooner than October 15, 2026\"; Anthropic gives at least 60 days notice; claude-sonnet-5-5 is Active until not sooner than 2027-09-28. Opus 5.5 (Work Map) is Active until not sooner than 2027-09-22. Nothing retires inside Phase 0, but the fallback must be real, not a memory note.\nWhat:\n1. `src/lib/models.ts`: one place for the defaults and the fallback: `VISION_MODEL_DEFAULT = \"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\"`, `DECIDE_MODEL_DEFAULT` same, `FALLBACK_MODEL = \"claude-sonnet-5-5\"`, `WORKMAP_MODEL_DEFAULT = \"claude-opus-5-5\"`, `resolveModel(kind)` reading VISION_MODEL / DECIDE_MODEL / WORKMAP_MODEL env. The vision (src/lib/perception/vision.ts) and decide LLM (src/lib/decide/*.ts) callers use it. When the API answers 404 with an error type `not_found_error` for the model, or the model id is in a `RETIRED_MODELS` list in models.ts, retry once with FALLBACK_MODEL and log a warn line; no infinite loop.\n2. Tests: vision and decide suites pass with VISION_MODEL/DECIDE_MODEL set to claude-sonnet-5-5 (parametrise the existing mocked-fetch tests over both ids, asserting the model in the request body); the 404 fallback path retries once with FALLBACK_MODEL.\n3. docs/checks/models.md: the dated check (2026-10-06, status table rows for the three models), the env names, how to switch in Vercel, and when to re-check (monthly, and on any Anthropic deprecation email).\nVision route file src/app/api/vision/route.ts is owned by another task: do not edit it (only lib files). No new dependencies. Do not touch README.md, docs/DEPLOY.md, .env.example.",
